{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/UsingIvorABC","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivorabc\/usingivorabc"]}],"metadata":{"title":"Using IvorABC","role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"IvorABC"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Take ABC text from "},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to a validated syntax tree, and back to "},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IvorABC exposes four processing types. Each is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" value type with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no-argument initializer and a single primary method:"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Type","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Method","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Result","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCParser","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parse(_:)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(ABCTunebook, [ABCParser.Diagnostic])"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCNormalizer","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"normalize(_:)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(ABCTunebook, [ABCNormalizer.Change])"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCValidator","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"validate(_:)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(ABCTunebook, [ABCValidator.Issue])"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCFormatter","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"format(_:)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data"}]}]]],"header":"row","alignments":["left","left","left"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCTunebook"},{"type":"text","text":" carries two Boolean state flags that enforce the order of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pipeline:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isNormalized"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"validate(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" throws unless this is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isValidated"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"format(_:)"},{"text":" throws unless this is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So the canonical order is "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"parse → normalize → validate → format"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let (parsed, diagnostics) = try ABCParser().parse(data)","let (normalized, changes) = ABCNormalizer().normalize(parsed)","let (validated, issues)   = try ABCValidator().validate(normalized)","","guard issues.isEmpty","else { \/* handle issues *\/ return }","","let output = try ABCFormatter().format(validated)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"normalize(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"validate(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are idempotent — calling them on a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tunebook that is already normalized or validated returns it unchanged — so it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"always safe to run the full pipeline."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Parsing","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Parsing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCParser","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" decodes UTF-8 "},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" into an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCTunebook","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let (tunebook, diagnostics) = try ABCParser().parse(data)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The parser chooses its own parse policy from the version declared in the input:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"strict"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" for files that declare ABC 2.1 or later, and "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"loose"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" for everything"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"else (including unversioned files). In loose mode it recovers from common"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deviations rather than failing, and reports each recovery — along with any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deprecated forms accepted in either mode — as an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCParser\/Diagnostic","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Diagnostics are always returned, never thrown; each has a human-readable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"message","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["for diagnostic in diagnostics {","    print(diagnostic.message)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Diagnostics cover recoverable situations such as a deprecated tempo form"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"Q:120","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), a duplicate "},{"code":"%%abc-charset","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", an unrecognized character set, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"malformed version string, or a skipped unrecognizable line."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unrecoverable problems are thrown as an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCParser\/Error","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", for example"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":".invalidField(_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".invalidKeySignature(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".orphanedContinuation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":".unmatchedBeginDirective(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"code":".missingTunes","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Like all IvorABC errors it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conforms to "},{"code":"EnhancedError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and provides a "},{"code":"message","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["do {","    let (tunebook, _) = try ABCParser().parse(data)","} catch let error as ABCParser.Error {","    print(error.message)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Normalizing","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Normalizing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCNormalizer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" upgrades legacy and deprecated constructs to their ABC 2.1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"equivalents, returning a new tunebook whose "},{"code":"isNormalized","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" flag is "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose "},{"code":"version","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"ABCVersion.current","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", together with a list of the changes it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applied:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let (normalized, changes) = ABCNormalizer().normalize(tunebook)","","for change in changes {","    print(change.message)          \/\/ what was changed","    print(change.tuneIndex ?? -1)  \/\/ which tune, or nil for the file header","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Normalization performs conversions such as:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"E:"},{"type":"text","text":" (elemskip) and legacy "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"I:"},{"type":"text","text":" (information) fields → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"r:"},{"type":"text","text":" (remark)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Deprecated C-form tempos ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Q:C=rate"},{"type":"text","text":") resolved against the active "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"L:"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"M:"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"+name+"},{"type":"text","text":" decorations → the standard "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"!name!"},{"type":"text","text":" form."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dropping stale directives ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"%%abc-charset"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"%%abc-version"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"%%decoration +"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCNormalizer\/Change","isActive":true},{"text":" case (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clearedBeatMultiplier"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"convertedDecoration","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"removedDirective","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"replacedField"},{"type":"text","text":") carries the affected"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"value, so you can present a precise change log rather than just a count."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Validating","type":"heading","anchor":"Validating","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCValidator","isActive":true},{"text":" checks a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"normalized"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" tunebook against the ABC 2.1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specification:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let (validated, issues) = try ABCValidator().validate(normalized)","","if issues.isEmpty {","    \/\/ `validated.isValidated` is now true.","} else {","    issues.forEach { print($0.message) }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the tunebook has not been normalized, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"validate(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" throws"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCValidator\/Error\/notNormalized","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If any issues are found, the returned tunebook is the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"input unchanged"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isValidated"},{"type":"text","text":" flag stays "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":"). Fix the issues — or run it through the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"normalizer again after editing — and validate again."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Only when the issues array is empty does the returned tunebook have","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isValidated == true"},{"type":"text","text":" — the prerequisite for formatting."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCValidator\/Issue","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" describes a specific conformance problem — a missing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or misplaced "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"X:"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T:"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"K:"},{"type":"text","text":" field, an inline field used where it is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"allowed, more than one chord symbol or grace-note group on a single note, or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shorthand decoration with no defining "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"U:"},{"type":"text","text":" field — and exposes both a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"message"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tuneIndex"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Formatting","type":"heading","anchor":"Formatting","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCFormatter","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" serializes a "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"validated"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" tunebook back to ABC 2.1-compliant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"UTF-8 "},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let data = try ABCFormatter().format(validated)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the tunebook has not been validated, "},{"code":"format(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" throws"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCFormatter\/Error\/notValidated","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Because the model is validated first,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"formatting itself does not fail on content — round-tripping "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parse → normalize → validate → format"},{"type":"text","text":" reproduces a specification-compliant document."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The AST model","type":"heading","anchor":"The-AST-model","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The syntactic model is a tree of value types:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["ABCTunebook","├─ version:    ABCVersion?","├─ fileHeader: [ABCHeaderEntry]","└─ tunes:      [ABCTune]","   ├─ header: [ABCHeaderEntry]   \/\/ .directive | .field","   └─ body:   [ABCBodyEntry]     \/\/ .directive | .field | .symbols([ABCSymbol])"]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCField","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is an enum with one case per ABC information\/tune field"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".tuneTitle"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".key"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".meter"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".tempo"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".voice"},{"type":"text","text":", …). Each case’s payload"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a dedicated, fully-typed value (e.g. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".key(ABCKeySignature)"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCSymbol","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is an enum covering everything that can appear in a line of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"music: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".note"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".chord"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".rest"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".barLine"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".decoration"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".tuplet"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".slur"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".chordSymbol"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".inlineField"},{"type":"text","text":", and so on."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Leaf values are wrapped in small validating types — for instance "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCText","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCReferenceNumber","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCVoice\/ID-swift.struct","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCClef\/Name-swift.struct","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — each of which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exposes an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isValid(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" check and a failable initializer that returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for out-of-range input. Others, like "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCLength","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", validate internally in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"failable initializer without a public "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isValid(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" check. All AST types are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCTunebook","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" equality compares "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fileHeader"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tunes"},{"type":"text","text":" only;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isNormalized"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isValidated"},{"type":"text","text":" flags are metadata and are excluded."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Building a tunebook programmatically","type":"heading","anchor":"Building-a-tunebook-programmatically","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can construct the AST directly rather than parsing text. Leaf initializers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are failable, returning "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when their validity constraints are not met:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let refNumber = ABCReferenceNumber(uintValue: 1)!","let title     = ABCText(stringValue: \"Cooley's\")!","let key       = ABCKeySignature.standard(.init(tonic: .e,","                                               mode: .dorian)!)","","let header: [ABCHeaderEntry] = [","    .field(.referenceNumber(refNumber)),  \/\/ X:1","    .field(.tuneTitle(title)),            \/\/ T:Cooley's","    .field(.key(key)),                    \/\/ K:Edor","]","","let tune     = ABCTune(header: header,","                       body: [])!","let tunebook = ABCTunebook(fileHeader: [],","                           tunes: [tune])!"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A directly-constructed tunebook has "},{"code":"isNormalized == false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"isValidated == false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — exactly like one fresh out of the parser — so you must run it through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the normalizer and validator before formatting."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Error-handling","text":"Error handling"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Thrown errors conform to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EnhancedError"},{"text":" (from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/eBardX\/XestiTools","isActive":true},{"text":"): each has a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"category"},{"type":"text","text":" of"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"IvorABC\""},{"type":"text","text":" and a human-readable "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"message"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"table","alignments":["left","left"],"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Type"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Thrown by"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCParser\/Error","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ABCParser.parse(_:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCValidator\/Error","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ABCValidator.validate(_:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCFormatter\/Error","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ABCFormatter.format(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ABCNormalizer.normalize(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" never throws — normalization has no failure mode."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-fatal results are returned rather than thrown, and each also provides a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"message"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"table","alignments":["left","left"],"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Type"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returned by"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCParser\/Diagnostic","type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parse(_:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCNormalizer\/Change","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"normalize(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCValidator\/Issue","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"validate(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCNormalizer\/Change","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCValidator\/Issue","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" also expose a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tuneIndex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int?"},{"type":"text","text":"): the tune the result applies to, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" for the file header."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Concurrency","level":2,"anchor":"Concurrency"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IvorABC is built for Swift 6 strict concurrency. Every public type — the four"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"processing types and the entire AST — is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" value type, so instances"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be freely shared across tasks and actor boundaries. The processing types"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hold no mutable state, so a single "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCParser","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCNormalizer","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier